{"accounts":{"guide-entry-3f092d5f3838d3c3bec0853f":{"description":"1st session of the International Law Commission (1949) Formulation of the Principles recognized in the Charter of the Nürnberg Tribunal and in the Judgment of the Tribunal — The principles as stated by Sir Hartley Shawcross before the American Bar Association in 1946 A/CN.4/12 (in Yearbook, 1949 , part I, 17th meeting (9 May 1949))","document_locator":"part I, 17th meeting (9 May 1949","document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-3f092d5f3838d3c3bec0853f","section":"other"},"guide-entry-4307314453859054ba151923":{"description":"1st session of the International Law Commission (1949) The Charter and the Judgment of the Nürnberg Tribunal: History and Analysis A/CN.4/5 (U.N. publication, Sales No.: 1949.V.7)","document_locator":null,"document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-4307314453859054ba151923","section":"secretariat_and_secretary_general"},"guide-entry-521c1cc19a6145bf1e67a626":{"description":"Historical survey, resolutions of the United Nations concerning the formulation of the Nürnberg Principles, formulation of the Nürnberg Principles by the International Law Commission, the principles of International Law recognized in the Charter and the Judgment of the Nürnberg Tribunal: Texts and Comments, and the proposed text of the Nürnberg Principles as formulated by the International Law Commission. Report of the Special Rapporteur , Mr. Jean Spiropoulos ( 2nd session of the ILC (1950)) A/CN.4/22 (in Yearbook, 1950, vol. II) ILC Report, A/1316 (A/5/12), 1950, part III, para. 97","document_locator":"part III, para","document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-521c1cc19a6145bf1e67a626","section":"special_rapporteur"},"guide-entry-7339a97309dccfc5f6dead61":{"description":"International Law Commission ( 2nd session , 1950) Completed its consideration of the item and submitted its report to the General Assembly for its consideration, together with the principles of international law which were recognized in the Charter of the Nürnberg Tribunal and in the judgment of the Tribunal, together with comments thereon . ILC Report, A/1316 (A/5/12), 1950, part I, chap. I, paras. 13–14 Yearbook, 1950, vol. II","document_locator":"part I, chap","document_role":"related_evidence","entry_id":"guide-entry-7339a97309dccfc5f6dead61","section":"final_outcome"},"guide-entry-8bb5d6ca4331bd317f5647a5":{"description":"Formulation of the principles recognized in the Nürnberg Tribunal and in the Judgment of the Tribunal — Texts recommended by the Sub-Committee A/CN.4/W.12 (in Yearbook, 1949 , part I, 31st meeting (1 June 1949), ft.8) ILC Report, A/925 (A/4/10), 1949, part I, chap. III, paras. 28–9","document_locator":"part I, 31st meeting (1 June 1949","document_role":"reported_in","entry_id":"guide-entry-8bb5d6ca4331bd317f5647a5","section":"working_group_or_subcommittee"},"guide-entry-a3545e5f993b20c2d59e1d41":{"description":"Report of the International Law Commission on the work of its first session , 12 April 1949 to 9 June 1949 Decided that its task under resolution 177(II) was not to express any appreciation of the principles as principles of international law but merely to formulate principles of a substantive character. Decided to refer the draft to a rapporteur in order to prepare a report to be submitted to the Commission at its second session in 1950. Discussion in Plenary : 17th meeting (9 May 1949), 25th , 26th , 27th , 28th and 29th meetings (23 May to 27 May 1949), and 31st meeting (1 June 1949) ILC Report, A/925 (A/4/10), 1949, part I, chap. III, paras. 25–29 Yearbook, 1949 , part II Yearbook, 1949 , part I","document_locator":"part I, chap","document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-a3545e5f993b20c2d59e1d41","section":"ilc_report"},"guide-entry-cf115a14dc6b86ef28463221":{"description":"Report of the International Law Commission on the work of its second session , 5 June to 29 July 1950 On the basis of the report of the Special Rapporteur , the Commission adopted a formulation of the principles of international law which were recognized in the Charter of the Nürnberg Tribunal and in the judgment of the Tribunal, together with comments thereon . Discussion in Plenary : 44th , 45th , 46th , 47th , 48th and 49th meetings (12 to 19 June 1950) ILC Report, A/1316 (A/5/12), 1950, part III, paras. 95–127 Yearbook, 1950, vol. II Yearbook, 1950, vol. I","document_locator":"part III, paras","document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-cf115a14dc6b86ef28463221","section":"ilc_report"},"guide-entry-da5f7d30ac231fc857f8f445":{"description":"3rd session of the International Law Commission (1951) Observations of Member States on the Commission's formulation of the Nürnberg Principles A/CN.4/45, Add.1 and Add.2 (in Yearbook, 1951, vol. II) ILC Report, A/1858 (A/5/9), 1951, chap. IV, para. 57","document_locator":null,"document_role":"mentioned_in_description","entry_id":"guide-entry-da5f7d30ac231fc857f8f445","section":"government_comments"},"guide-entry-db86cd1d1cbeb7301640803a":{"description":"1st session of the International Law Commission (1949) Formulation of the principles recognized in the Nürnberg Tribunal and in the Judgment of the Tribunal — Draft proposed by the Sub-Committee on the formulation of the Nürnberg principles A/CN.4/W.6 (in Yearbook, 1949 , part I, 25th meeting (23 May 1949), ft.9) ILC Report, A/925 (A/4/10), 1949, part I, chap. III, paras. 28–9","document_locator":"part I, 25th meeting (23 May 1949","document_role":"reported_in","entry_id":"guide-entry-db86cd1d1cbeb7301640803a","section":"working_group_or_subcommittee"},"guide-entry-e3def000788ce273bf76ffdf":{"description":"Formulation of the Principles recognized in the Charter of the Nürnberg Tribunal and in the Judgment of the Tribunal — Proposal by Professor Georges Scelle A/CN.4/W.11 (in Yearbook, 1949 , part I, 28th meeting (26 May 1949)) ILC Report, A/925 (A/4/10), 1949, chap. III, para. 27","document_locator":